1
00:00:02,290 --> 00:00:04,220
《生活大爆炸》前情提要
Previously on The Big Bang Theory

2
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:06,450
谢尔顿  你这是想出了一个办法
Sheldon, did you just figure out a method

3
00:00:06,450 --> 00:00:09,350
可以人工合成一种新型稳定超重元素吗
for synthesizing a new stable super-heavy element?

4
00:00:09,350 --> 00:00:10,910
是吗
Did I?

5
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:12,540
这不可能呀
Well, that can't be right.

6
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:13,960
从来没有人成功过呢
No one's ever done that before.

7
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:15,810
除了我  我想出来了
Except me, because I just did it!

8
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:17,620
谢尔顿谢尔顿脑力无边
Sheldon and his brain-- yeah!

9
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:19,650
谢尔顿谢尔顿脑震八方
Sheldon and his brain-- yeah!

10
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:22,070
我犯了个可怕的错误
I've made a horrible mistake.

11
00:00:22,070 --> 00:00:23,410
你在说什么
What are you talking about?

12
00:00:23,410 --> 00:00:26,190
这个表格是平方厘米制的
This table-- it's in square centimeters.

13
00:00:26,190 --> 00:00:27,970
我看成了平方米
I read it as square meters.

14
00:00:27,970 --> 00:00:29,440
知道这意味着什么吗
You know what that means?

15
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:32,420
美国人看不懂公制吗
That Americans can't handle the metric system?

16
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:37,540
艾米  我这是失之毫厘差之千里的错误
Amy, I was off by a factor of 10,000.

17
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:39,770
但是中国研究小组发现了元素
But the Chinese team found the element.

18
00:00:39,770 --> 00:00:40,950
他们不应该发现的
Yeah, well, they shouldn't have.

19
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:42,730
我的计算是错的
My calculations were wrong.

20
00:00:42,730 --> 00:00:44,880
我这辈子最伟大的科学成就
the greatest scientific achievement of my life

21
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:46,370
是建立在一个巨大的错误之上
is based on a blunder.

22
00:00:46,370 --> 00:00:47,900
我不是天才
I'm not a genius,

23
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:49,770
我是个骗子
I'm a fraud.

24
00:00:50,370 --> 00:00:51,840
谢尔顿  在神经系统学里
You know, Sheldon, in neuroscience,

25
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,180
我们总是在大脑某处有所发现
we're forever finding something in one part of the brain

26
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:55,560
但地方和原来想的完全不一样
that we thought was someplace else.

27
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:58,760
这下可好  我连骗子都不如了
Oh, great, now I'm worse than a fraud.

28
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:00,990
我沦为生物学家之流了
I'm practically a biologist.

29
00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:02,890
时至今日

30
00:01:03,390 --> 00:01:05,610
欢迎收听《科学星期五》  我是艾拉·菲莱
This is Science Friday. I'm Ira Flatow.

31
00:01:05,610 --> 00:01:08,320
今日的来宾是第一个
My guest today is responsible for the discovery

32
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:11,080
稳定超重元素的发现者
of the first stable super-heavy element.

33
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:13,010
欢迎谢尔顿·库伯博士
Welcome, Dr. Sheldon Cooper.

34
00:01:13,010 --> 00:01:14,500
谢谢
Thank you.

35
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:16,760
是学校硬要我来的
Uh, the university made me come here.

36
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:18,190
我本人并不想来
I didn't want to.

37
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:21,040
我是这节目的忠实听众哦
Uh, big fan of the show.

38
00:01:22,860 --> 00:01:25,150
我听说你之所以发现这元素
So, I understand that you actually discovered

39
00:01:25,150 --> 00:01:27,360
完全是因为一个错误
this element by mistake.

40
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:29,970
是的
Yes.

41
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:33,890
而科学界有些人把这个错误称之为
And some people in the science community are calling it

42
00:01:33,890 --> 00:01:36,140
-"蠢货奇迹"  -那些人是谁
- "The Wonder Blunder." - Who?

43
00:01:36,140 --> 00:01:37,390
告诉我他们的名字
Give me their names.

44
00:01:37,390 --> 00:01:39,420
肯定是沃罗威茨
I bet it's Wolowitz.

45
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:42,000
这故事真是太了不起了
It's just such a fascinating story.

46
00:01:42,030 --> 00:01:43,840
你在计算上偏差了这么多
Your calculations are way off,

47
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,680
却还是有人找到了这元素
but they find the element anyway.

48
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:48,210
感觉就像是读错藏宝地图
It's like misreading a treasure map

49
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:50,770
却还是找到了宝藏一样
and still finding the treasure.

50
00:01:50,770 --> 00:01:52,450
我们能聊别的话题吗
Can we talk about something else?

51
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:55,170
你知道我会唱山歌吗
Do you know that I yodel?

52
00:01:56,930 --> 00:01:58,890
那不错啊  但这发现有可能
That's interesting, but this could be taking you

53
00:01:58,890 --> 00:02:01,540
让你获得诺贝尔奖
down the path toward a Nobel Prize.

54
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:03,630
而且是化学奖哦
And in chemistry, no less.

55
00:02:03,630 --> 00:02:04,930
这种情况很少见吧
And wouldn't that be unusual?

56
00:02:04,930 --> 00:02:07,030
因为你是物理学家
Because you're a physicist.

57
00:02:07,030 --> 00:02:09,750
对对对  我将是获得诺贝尔化学奖的物理学家
Yes, yes, I'd be a physicist with a Nobel in chemistry.

58
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:11,910
大家快来笑我这个奇葩吧
Everyone laugh at the circus freak.

59
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:15,620
我不需要坐在这忍受你的羞辱  菲莱
You know, I don't need to sit here and take this, Flatow.

60
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:18,060
就是因为有你这种恶霸
It is because of bullies like you,

61
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:19,560
所以每天才会有越来越多的
every day more and more Americans

62
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:21,910
美国人转投看电视
are making the switch to television.

63
00:02:48,270 --> 00:02:50,810
塞伯特校长  你为什么要凶我
President Seibert, I don't know why you're yelling.

64
00:02:50,810 --> 00:02:53,130
是你叫我去上广播节目的
You're the one who made me go on the radio.

65
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:56,160
我以为那会是一场专业的科学访谈
I was expecting a professional science interview,

66
00:02:56,160 --> 00:03:00,550
而不是被整人节目口无遮拦的主持人攻击
not an attack by some morning zoo shock jock.

67
00:03:00,910 --> 00:03:03,200
如果学校这么缺钱
Well, if the university needs money so badly,

68
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:05,690
或许你该设立个脏话罚款筒赚钱
perhaps you should start a swear jar.

69
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:09,390
你这一串脏话够罚一块钱啊
That one's worth a dollar.

70
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:12,810
我知道你不喜欢上节目
I know you don't like it,

71
00:03:12,810 --> 00:03:14,330
但是你每次去接受采访
but every time you do an interview,

72
00:03:14,330 --> 00:03:16,370
都能提大学提高知名度
it raises the profile of the university.

73
00:03:16,370 --> 00:03:17,960
高知名度就有高资助费
That translates to funding.

74
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,890
我又不是受训的卖艺猴子
Yeah, well, I'm not just some trained monkey

75
00:03:19,890 --> 00:03:21,710
帮他们乞讨钱
dancing for coins.

76
00:03:22,730 --> 00:03:23,870
你当然不是啦
Of course you're not.

77
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:25,690
那种猴子多讨人喜欢
People love trained monkeys.

78
00:03:27,780 --> 00:03:29,120
你有什么好不开心的啊
How can you not be happy?

79
00:03:29,150 --> 00:03:31,120
你又高又瘦又出名
You're tall, thin and famous.

80
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:33,780
天啊  我好嫉妒谢尔顿
Oh, my God, I'm jealous of Sheldon.

81
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:37,000
这些访谈估计还持续一段时间
Look, you're gonna be doing this stuff for a while.

82
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,440
你得找到习惯这些事的方法
You're just gonna have to find a way to get used to it.

83
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:41,330
但你们没人能懂我的心情
But none of you know what this is like.

84
00:03:41,330 --> 00:03:44,360
自己悔恨不已的事却被人大肆赞扬
Being celebrated for something you wish you never did.

85
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:47,720
想必你没跟我一起去过狂欢节
Mmm... you clearly haven't been with me at Mardi Gras.

86
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:53,400
要暂停一下游戏来帮忙我打扫吗
Want to pause the video game and help me clean up?

87
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,350
我正在打扫啊
I am cleaning up.

88
00:03:54,350 --> 00:03:56,870
打扫小丑对高谭市造成的破坏
Look at the mess the Joker made of Gotham City.

89
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:00,860
拜托  要来暂住的可是你的朋友
Come on, it's your friend who's coming to stay here.

90
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:02,150
拉杰是在印度长大的
Raj grew up in India.

91
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:04,180
相信我  比这更脏的他都见过
Trust me, he's seen worse.

92
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:06,300
华仔
Howie.

93
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,920
我保证这周接下来的日子我会帮忙
I promise I'll help out the rest of the week.

94
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:09,810
这周接下来的日子
The rest of the week?

95
00:04:09,810 --> 00:04:11,430
你不是说就一两天吗
You said it was just gonna be a night or two.

96
00:04:11,430 --> 00:04:12,540
但如果我直接跟你说住一周
Yeah, but if I told you a week,

97
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:14,060
-你会同意吗  -当然不会
- would you have said yes? - No!

98
00:04:14,060 --> 00:04:16,250
所以我只好出此下策啦
Then you left me no choice.

99
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:20,980
我喜欢拉杰  但他这暂住也太久了吧
I love Raj, but that's a long time for a house guest.

100
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:22,570
但他的公寓整个楼都在除虫  没法住
I know, but they're tenting his building.

101
00:04:22,570 --> 00:04:25,220
他也找不到能让带宠物的酒店
He can't find a hotel he likes that allows dogs.

102
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,550
他还带小桂子来啊
He's bringing Cinnamon?

103
00:04:26,550 --> 00:04:27,570
待一整周呢
For a whole week!

104
00:04:27,570 --> 00:04:29,340
有些人真是大惊小怪
The nerve of some people.

105
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:36,530
迎面而来的是羞愧号快车
Here comes the Embarrassment Express.

106
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:39,700
将会经过  骗子镇站
With stops at Fraudville...

107
00:04:39,700 --> 00:04:42,220
蠢货奇迹山站
WonderBlunderberg...

108
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:45,040
以及堪萨斯城
and Kansas City.

109
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:47,350
只因这是运输交汇处
Because it's a hub.

110
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:50,200
谢尔顿  我能进来吧
Sheldon, can I come in?

111
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:51,710
-你有带饼干吗  -没有
- Do you have cookies? - No.

112
00:04:51,710 --> 00:04:53,850
很好  我不配吃饼干  进来吧
Good. I don't deserve cookies. Come in.

113
00:04:56,440 --> 00:04:58,080
-威尔...  -谢尔顿
- Wil...? - Hey, Sheldon.

114
00:04:58,080 --> 00:04:59,310
好久不见
It's been a while.

115
00:04:59,310 --> 00:05:00,590
你怎么来了
Why are you here?

116
00:05:00,590 --> 00:05:02,070
艾米说你最近不开心
Amy said you were having a rough time,

117
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:03,230
我就想来开导开导你
and I thought maybe we could talk.

118
00:05:03,230 --> 00:05:04,470
可以吗
Is that okay?

119
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:05,940
当然可以
Certainly.

120
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:06,740
虽然...
Although...

121
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:08,130
现在我就不开心
right now, I'm having a rough time

122
00:05:08,130 --> 00:05:09,840
因为我房间现在有三个人
because there's three people in my room,

123
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:12,760
感觉跟迪斯科舞厅一样拥挤
and it's starting to feel like a discotheque.

124
00:05:14,220 --> 00:05:16,420
谢尔顿  你说你不开心是因为
Sheldon, you said you were unhappy getting attention

125
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:18,690
人们都在关注让你悔恨不已的事
for something you wished you never did.

126
00:05:18,690 --> 00:05:20,620
关于这事  我也有点经验
Yeah, I know a little something about that.

127
00:05:20,890 --> 00:05:22,800
少来了  威尔
Oh, nonsense, Wil.

128
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:25,700
你的刷屏微博也没那么糟啦
Your endless tweets are not that bad.

129
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:29,140
我想起这么久不见他的原因了
I remember why it's been a while.

130
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:31,270
谢尔顿  我要说的是
Sheldon, I was actually talking

131
00:05:31,270 --> 00:05:33,400
我小时候在星际迷航里演出的事
about when I was a kid on Star Trek.

132
00:05:33,830 --> 00:05:35,310
你怎么会不喜欢因为出演该电影
How could you not like getting attention

133
00:05:35,310 --> 00:05:36,850
而获得大家的关注呢
for playing Wesley Crusher?

134
00:05:36,850 --> 00:05:38,270
你的角色很讨喜啊
You were wonderful.

135
00:05:38,750 --> 00:05:42,210
一个全知全能记忆超强的男孩
A know-it-all boy genius with an eidetic memory.

136
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:44,580
谁对那个角色会没有代入感啊
Who couldn't relate to that?

137
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,110
不是每个人都这么想的
Well, not everybody felt that way.

138
00:05:47,110 --> 00:05:48,870
很多人很讨厌那个角色
A lot of people really hated the character,

139
00:05:48,870 --> 00:05:51,110
因此有些人也为此而讨厌我
and some of them hated me because of it.

140
00:05:51,110 --> 00:05:52,190
我也曾接受过访谈
I would do interviews,

141
00:05:52,190 --> 00:05:54,130
很多人都会嘲讽我
and people would be mean to me.

142
00:05:54,130 --> 00:05:56,170
我也碰到这种事了
That just happened to me.

143
00:05:56,170 --> 00:05:57,770
下次你想不出刷什么屏了
Next time you're stuck for a tweet,

144
00:05:57,770 --> 00:06:00,880
欢迎你写一条艾拉·菲莱是混蛋的微博
feel free to say what a jerk Ira Flatow is.

145
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:05,440
谢尔顿  重点的是威尔能学会接受现实
Sheldon, the point is Wil learned to embrace that part of his life

146
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:08,070
然后更重要的东西迈进
and moved on to bigger and better things.

147
00:06:08,070 --> 00:06:09,220
是啊  我现在是个作家
Yeah, I'm an author now,

148
00:06:09,220 --> 00:06:10,420
经常公开演讲
I do public speaking,

149
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:13,230
我自己还出了一部关于桌游的网络剧
and I have my own web series about board games.

150
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:16,550
我们是要哄他开心  所以...
We're trying to cheer him up, so...

151
00:06:21,650 --> 00:06:23,400
我只是想告诉你  曾有一段时间
I'm just saying that there was a time when I thought

152
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:25,720
我以为自己走不出那角色的阴影
I would never get out of Wesley Crusher's shadow.

153
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:26,550
但现在
But now,

154
00:06:26,550 --> 00:06:29,310
那只是我完美人生中的一小章节
it's just one small part of a pretty great life,

155
00:06:29,310 --> 00:06:31,850
我也很开心有过那些经历
and it's a part that I'm happy is there.

156
00:06:31,850 --> 00:06:34,020
我明白你的意思
I do see what you're saying.

157
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:35,350
挺受用的
That helps.

158
00:06:35,350 --> 00:06:36,580
那就好
Good.

159
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:38,790
你们俩个要留下来一起玩火车吗
Would you two like to stay and play trains with me?

160
00:06:38,790 --> 00:06:39,670
-好  -可以啊
- Sure. - Okay.

161
00:06:39,670 --> 00:06:41,050
太好了
Oh, great!

162
00:06:41,570 --> 00:06:42,660
现在呢
Now...

163
00:06:43,930 --> 00:06:45,080
我来操作控制器
I work the controls.

164
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:46,330
我来喊"请上车"
I say "All aboard",

165
00:06:46,330 --> 00:06:48,800
你们俩安静坐着看就行了
you sit quietly and watch.

166
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:51,400
我能吹哨子吗
Can I blow the whistle?

167
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:55,210
你还是走吧
You should probably go.

168
00:07:02,820 --> 00:07:04,590
你要在我家沙发上刷牙吗
You're gonna brush your teeth on my couch?

169
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:06,880
我是要刷小桂子的牙
No, I'm gonna brush Cinnamon's teeth.

170
00:07:07,890 --> 00:07:08,660
何苦呢
Why bother?

171
00:07:08,660 --> 00:07:11,070
她有一半的时间都是在舔屁眼
She spends half the time licking her butt.

172
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:13,690
另一半的时间是在舔我脸
And the other half licking my face.

173
00:07:13,690 --> 00:07:15,370
所以我才要帮她刷牙
That's why I'm brushing her teeth.

174
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:19,530
抱歉  我回来晚了
Hey, guys. Sorry I'm so late.

175
00:07:19,530 --> 00:07:20,480
你们吃完饭了吗
Did you already have dinner?

176
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:22,230
没  我们在等你
No, we were waiting for you.

177
00:07:22,230 --> 00:07:23,580
你们真好
Aw, that's so sweet.

178
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:25,860
所以你今晚打算煮什么呢
Yeah. So what do you feel like making?

179
00:07:27,210 --> 00:07:29,800
霍华德  这可怜的姑娘刚忙完回家
Howard, the poor thing just got home from work.

180
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:31,770
我先给你倒杯酒
Let me get you a glass of wine.

181
00:07:31,770 --> 00:07:32,750
然后我来做晚餐
I'll cook dinner.

182
00:07:32,750 --> 00:07:35,150
-拉杰  你可是客人  -没关系啦
- Oh, Raj, you're our guest. - Don't be silly.

183
00:07:35,150 --> 00:07:37,180
快坐下  你看上去很累
Sit. You look like you've had a long day.

184
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:39,990
没事啦  她经常这样
No, she always looks like that.

185
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:45,400
因为她嫁了个傻逼
Because she married an idiot.

186
00:07:47,430 --> 00:07:48,680
谢谢  拉杰
Thank you, Raj.

187
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:51,900
客气啥  就当是我感谢你们
Please, this is my way of thanking you

188
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:53,380
让我住在这里吧
for letting me stay here.

189
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:56,520
跟我们说说你今天过得怎么样
Now, tell us all about your day.

190
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:58,810
好的  首先我开会迟到了
Okay, um, well, first, I was late to a meeting

191
00:07:58,810 --> 00:07:59,890
因为在路上堵车了
'cause I was stuck in traffic.

192
00:07:59,890 --> 00:08:02,240
我就叫你在手机装一个交通实时监控软件嘛
Well, I keep telling you to put that traffic app on your phone.

193
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:05,020
你今天回家抱怨  因为吃太多糖豆
Hey, when you got home today complaining that you felt sick

194
00:08:05,020 --> 00:08:06,370
而肚子不舒服时
from eating too many jelly beans,

195
00:08:06,370 --> 00:08:07,650
我有教你怎么解决问题吗
did I tell you how to fix it?

196
00:08:07,650 --> 00:08:09,250
没有
No.

197
00:08:10,130 --> 00:08:11,840
相反  我说"小可怜  一定很疼吧"
I said, "Aw, that must hurt,"

198
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:14,140
然后帮你揉肚肚
and I rubbed your belly.

199
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:20,000
我全程都在想着你
I thought of you the whole time.

200
00:08:22,880 --> 00:08:25,450
我的意思是  有时你只需去倾听
All I'm saying is there's a time to just listen.

201
00:08:25,450 --> 00:08:26,280
多谢
Thank you.

202
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:28,540
有时你也得适可而止  别吃那么多糖豆
There's also a time to stop eating too many jelly beans.

203
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:30,650
"有时"是指十岁以后
And it's when you're ten.

204
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:35,170
塞伯特校长
Hello, President Siebert.

205
00:08:35,170 --> 00:08:36,680
谢谢您接听我的电话
Thank you for taking my call.

206
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:40,070
我只是想让您知道  您现在可以指望我
I just wanted you to know that you can now expect

207
00:08:40,070 --> 00:08:43,330
热心参与有关我的发现的一切活动了
enthusiastic participation from me regarding my discovery.

208
00:08:43,670 --> 00:08:44,520
不  不  不
Oh, no, no, no, no.

209
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:45,690
无需感谢我
No need to thank me.

210
00:08:45,690 --> 00:08:48,680
要谢就谢我的朋友  威尔·惠顿
Thank my friend, Wil Wheaton.

211
00:08:49,210 --> 00:08:51,870
向您报告一下  我有九个朋友
For your information, I have nine friends, hmm?

212
00:08:53,470 --> 00:08:55,700
算上您的话  就十个
Ten if we include you.

213
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:58,430
那就九个吧
Nine it is.

214
00:09:01,660 --> 00:09:04,800
还是十个吧  算上沃罗威茨好了
Ah, it's ten. I'll count Wolowitz.

215
00:09:06,070 --> 00:09:07,510
你好  朋友莱纳德
Hello, friend Leonard.

216
00:09:07,510 --> 00:09:08,870
你心情不错嘛
Hey, you're in a good mood.

217
00:09:08,870 --> 00:09:10,610
我心情超棒的
I'm in a great mood.

218
00:09:10,610 --> 00:09:12,980
那你的心情即将变得更棒
Well, you're about to be in an even better one.

219
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:14,670
我是现在确定了才敢告诉你
I didn't want to say anything until I knew for sure,

220
00:09:14,670 --> 00:09:15,480
但
but...

221
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:18,280
我在我实验室重新测试了你的元素
I've been re-running the tests on your element in my lab

222
00:09:18,590 --> 00:09:19,680
我证明了它不存在
and I disproved it.

223
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:22,290
你的元素根本不存在
Your element does not exist!

224
00:09:22,750 --> 00:09:24,570
是吗  但中国的研究小组呢
Yeah, but what about the Chinese research team?

225
00:09:24,570 --> 00:09:25,520
他们的确发现了啊
They found it.

226
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:26,980
结果证明是有人在
Yeah, it turns out someone added

227
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:29,200
数据文件里加入了模拟信号
simulated signals to the data files.

228
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:31,070
他们伪造了结果
They faked the results.

229
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:32,740
-真的吗  -真的
- Really? - Yes!

230
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:33,590
你知道这意味着什么吗
Do you know what that means?

231
00:09:33,590 --> 00:09:36,830
你讨厌的所有关注  通通都会消失
That means all of this attention that you hate goes away.

232
00:09:36,830 --> 00:09:37,960
所以不会再有访问吗
So no more interviews?

233
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:39,080
对  全都结束了
No, it's all over.

234
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:40,100
真是难以置信
I can't believe it.

235
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:40,990
不用客气
Well, you're welcome.

236
00:09:40,990 --> 00:09:43,860
你夺走了我这辈子最大的成就
You robbed me of my greatest achievement!

237
00:09:45,450 --> 00:09:46,220
什么
What?!

238
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:48,720
我现在只有九个朋友了
I'm back down to nine friends!

239
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:51,990
算了  八个吧  我也不喜欢沃罗威茨
Make it eight-- I'm sick of Wolowitz, too!

240
00:09:53,070 --> 00:09:54,660
我不明白了
I-I don't understand.

241
00:09:54,660 --> 00:09:56,330
自从你发现这个该死的元素后
All you've done since you discovered

242
00:09:56,330 --> 00:09:57,750
你就一直在抱怨个不停
this stupid element was complain.

243
00:09:57,750 --> 00:09:59,200
我只是想让你开心
I was trying to make you happy!

244
00:09:59,460 --> 00:10:01,850
所以要夺走我唯一成名的机会吗
By taking away my only claim to fame?

245
00:10:01,850 --> 00:10:03,450
如果你想让我开心
Well, if you wanted to make me happy,

246
00:10:03,450 --> 00:10:04,750
你可以跟我讲个笑话
you could have told me a joke.

247
00:10:04,750 --> 00:10:06,910
或是给我看一段有爱的视频
Or shown me a cute video

248
00:10:06,910 --> 00:10:08,230
比如考拉和水獭
of a koala and an otter

249
00:10:08,230 --> 00:10:10,230
破天荒地成为朋友
becoming unlikely friends.

250
00:10:10,230 --> 00:10:13,170
你总是最有理那个
Oh, there is no winning with you.

251
00:10:13,170 --> 00:10:15,420
而且考拉和水獭居住地差了十万八千里
And koalas and otters don't even live near each other!

252
00:10:15,420 --> 00:10:18,690
所以它们成为朋友才是破天荒之举
That's what makes their friendship unlikely!

253
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:21,420
你们俩在吵什么啊
What's with all the yelling?

254
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:23,430
莱纳德推翻了我的发现
Leonard disproved my element.

255
00:10:23,430 --> 00:10:25,640
现在所有的关注都要消失了
Now all the attention is going to go away.

256
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:27,240
这很好啊  你一定很激动吧
Oh, that's great. You must be thrilled!

257
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:30,390
很好  我现在只剩七个朋友了
That's it! I'm down to seven friends.

258
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:34,690
他是连霍比特人和超级英雄都算上了吧
He's counting hobbits and superheroes, right?

259
00:10:35,130 --> 00:10:37,550
一开始我以为元素是真实存在的  我不想要它
When I thought the element was real, I didn't want it.

260
00:10:37,550 --> 00:10:39,570
但现在莱纳德证实它并不存在
But now that Leonard made it not exist,

261
00:10:39,570 --> 00:10:41,690
它反而成了我全世界最想要的东西了
I want it more than anything in the world.

262
00:10:41,690 --> 00:10:43,510
那元素从来就不存在
The-the element never existed.

263
00:10:43,510 --> 00:10:45,450
不是我夺走它  而是科学夺走了它
I didn't take it away, science took it away.

264
00:10:45,450 --> 00:10:46,610
要气就气科学吧
Be mad at science.

265
00:10:46,610 --> 00:10:49,620
你胆敢用科学来反驳我
Don't you dare use science against me.

266
00:10:50,060 --> 00:10:51,880
科学可是我最好的朋友
Science is my best friend!

267
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:53,770
太好了  我又有八个朋友了
Oh, good, I'm back up to eight.

268
00:10:55,030 --> 00:10:57,010
你能告诉他  他疯了吗
Will you tell him he's out of his mind.

269
00:10:57,010 --> 00:10:58,320
老实说  我理解他的意思
Actually, I get what he's saying.

270
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,600
太棒了  变九个了
Oh, yes! Nine!

271
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,600
欢迎回来  朋友
Welcome back, buddy.

272
00:11:03,270 --> 00:11:05,320
就像跟一个你不是很喜欢的人约会
It's like if you're dating someone you're not that into,

273
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:06,290
等那人跟你分手了
and then they break up with you

274
00:11:06,290 --> 00:11:07,600
你就变得很想要那人了
and then you want them more than ever.

275
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:09,540
我完全不知道她在说什么
I have no idea what she's talking about.

276
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:13,120
但我们现在联手对付你  所以我赞成她的话
but we're ganged up on you so I agree.

277
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:15,790
谢尔顿  那你要我怎么样
Okay, Sheldon, what do you want me to do,

278
00:11:15,790 --> 00:11:17,230
隐瞒我的发现吗
hide the information?

279
00:11:17,230 --> 00:11:18,100
如果我不公布
If I don't publish it,

280
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:20,140
迟早其他人也会这么做的
it's just a matter of time before someone else does.

281
00:11:20,140 --> 00:11:21,910
不  你当然得公布
No, no, of course you have to publish.

282
00:11:21,910 --> 00:11:23,770
那是你作为一个科学家应尽的责任
That's your responsibility as a scientist.

283
00:11:23,770 --> 00:11:25,570
否则会违背职业道德
Doing otherwise would be unethical.

284
00:11:25,570 --> 00:11:27,560
你别无选择
You have no choice.

285
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:28,580
好吧  我会公布
Fine, I'll publish.

286
00:11:28,580 --> 00:11:30,380
你看这没良心的混球
Can you believe this guy?

287
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:38,870
拉杰把碗都洗了
Aw! Raj did the dishes.

288
00:11:38,870 --> 00:11:40,240
你怎么知道不是我洗的
How do you know I didn't do them?

289
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:41,850
因为有一次  所有刀子都没洗
Because once, when all the knives were dirty,

290
00:11:41,850 --> 00:11:44,260
你宁愿用钥匙切面包圈  也懒得洗
you cut a bagel with your keys.

291
00:11:45,940 --> 00:11:48,130
早上好  两位
Good morning, everybody.

292
00:11:48,130 --> 00:11:50,260
我出去的时候  顺便买了咖啡
I picked up coffee while I was out.

293
00:11:50,260 --> 00:11:53,300
伯纳黛特  这是你的大豆薄荷摩卡
Bernadette, here's your soy peppermint mocha.

294
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:54,640
你真是太客气了
Aw, you didn't have to do that.

295
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:55,390
乐意之至
Oh, my pleasure,

296
00:11:55,390 --> 00:11:57,440
对了  不要担心今天的演讲
and don't worry about your presentation today.

297
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:58,490
你一定会表现出色
You're gonna be great.

298
00:11:58,490 --> 00:12:00,560
对啊  你一定能震惊四座
Yeah, you're gonna knock it out of the park.

299
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:02,930
我今天要做什么演讲来着
What presentation do I have today?

300
00:12:04,330 --> 00:12:04,990
快走吧
Just go.

301
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:11,520
他很爱你的
He loves you.

302
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:12,230
你这是干什么
What are you doing?

303
00:12:12,230 --> 00:12:13,780
你是故意让我难堪吗
Are you trying to make me look bad?

304
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:14,920
我只是想当个好客人
I'm just being a good house guest.

305
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:16,720
不  你是想当一个比我还好的丈夫
No, you're being a better husband than I am.

306
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:18,420
洗碗  买咖啡
Doing the dishes, getting coffee,

307
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:19,920
对她的生活了如指掌
knowing about her life--

308
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:21,260
谁会那样做啊
who does that?

309
00:12:22,660 --> 00:12:24,180
别这样嘛  我也给你买了一杯
Oh, come on, I brought you one, too.

310
00:12:24,180 --> 00:12:26,010
我不想喝咖啡
I don't want coffee.

311
00:12:26,010 --> 00:12:27,310
所以我给你买了热巧克力
That's why I got you hot chocolate.

312
00:12:27,310 --> 00:12:28,790
快给我
Give me that.

313
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:32,120
不许什么都做得比我好
Just stop showing me up.

314
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:33,690
霍华德  听我说
Howard, listen to me.

315
00:12:33,690 --> 00:12:35,320
你是一个很棒的丈夫
You're a great husband.

316
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:37,910
没错  你倾听的技巧还需要多练练
Yes, your listening skills could use some work.

317
00:12:37,910 --> 00:12:40,190
但作为一个独生子
But it's amazing how far you've come

318
00:12:40,190 --> 00:12:41,950
还有一个过度保护的老妈
given that you're an only child

319
00:12:41,950 --> 00:12:45,070
你算做得很不错啦
raised by an over-protective mom.

320
00:12:45,070 --> 00:12:46,760
这情形好像有点奇怪啊
Um, is this getting weird?

321
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:48,300
别动
Hang on.

322
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:54,840
的确是很怪
So, yes.

323
00:12:58,490 --> 00:13:01,350
我想告诉你一声  我发表了我的发现
I just wanted to let you know that I-I posted my findings.

324
00:13:01,580 --> 00:13:02,890
我看见了
I saw.

325
00:13:02,890 --> 00:13:05,880
我刚发公告  要求撤回我的论文
And I just posted a retraction of my paper.

326
00:13:05,880 --> 00:13:08,910
现在整个科学界都知道我是错的
Now the whole scientific community knows I was wrong.

327
00:13:08,910 --> 00:13:11,100
这样的事情经常发生  谢尔顿
These things happen all the time, Sheldon.

328
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:12,680
不是发生在我身上
Not to me.

329
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:14,590
我之前唯一一次公告的撤回说明
The only other retraction I ever had to issue

330
00:13:14,590 --> 00:13:17,410
还是在我7岁的时候  我承认我哥哥
was when I was seven and I conceded that my brother

331
00:13:17,410 --> 00:13:20,320
是东德州最优秀的忍者
was the greatest ninja in East Texas.

332
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:22,280
但那只是把我的脸
But that was just a ploy

333
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:24,330
从他的臭腋窝里拯救出来的权宜之计
to get my face out of his armpit.

334
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:28,100
他在这里啊
There he is!

335
00:13:28,550 --> 00:13:30,200
我最爱的超级英雄
It's my favorite superhero--

336
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:32,040
撤回侠
the Retractor!

337
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:36,350
拜托  别落井下石了
Come on, don't give him a hard time.

338
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:37,980
对不起  库珀
I'm sorry, Cooper.

339
00:13:37,980 --> 00:13:39,980
我撤回刚才说的话
I retract it.

340
00:13:41,090 --> 00:13:42,880
顺便说下  霍夫斯塔德
By the way, Hofstadter,

341
00:13:42,880 --> 00:13:45,420
做得真棒  推翻了中国研究组的结果
nice job disproving the Chinese team.

342
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:46,360
不算什么
It's not a big deal.

343
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:48,550
这可是大事
It's a huge deal.

344
00:13:48,550 --> 00:13:51,290
库珀  也许你不太适合研究物理
Cooper, maybe physics just isn't your thing.

345
00:13:51,290 --> 00:13:53,760
有没有考虑转去做零售
Have you ever considered a career in retail?

346
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:56,610
这样你就能靠撤回东西过生活了
That way you could take things back for a living.

347
00:13:58,160 --> 00:13:59,420
好了  巴里  太过了
Okay, Barry, that's enough.

348
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:00,980
不  没事
Oh, no, that's okay.

349
00:14:00,980 --> 00:14:03,180
我可以打赢自己的战斗
I can fight my own battles.

350
00:14:03,180 --> 00:14:06,420
对吗  "八尼"
Isn't that right, "Bawwy."

351
00:14:08,730 --> 00:14:09,710
你这是
Is...?

352
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:12,790
在嘲笑我的语言障碍吗
Is that a reference to my speech impediment?

353
00:14:13,890 --> 00:14:15,890
太伤人了
That's pretty hurtful.

354
00:14:16,530 --> 00:14:17,700
我
I...

355
00:14:18,100 --> 00:14:20,480
我自己没法控制
I can't control it.

356
00:14:21,390 --> 00:14:22,200
你说得对
You're right,

357
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:24,510
这招太卑鄙了
That was uncalled for.

358
00:14:24,510 --> 00:14:25,780
我收回
I take it back.

359
00:14:25,780 --> 00:14:26,550
你当然要收回了
Of course you do.

360
00:14:26,550 --> 00:14:28,940
因为你是鼎鼎大名的撤回侠
Because you're the Retractor!

361
00:14:33,270 --> 00:14:35,130
